demo-capture self-test
  ok a valid screenplay parses
  ok a region string resolves to whole pixels
  ok typing gets a default pace rather than instant text
  ok emphasis leads the action, so the zoom has arrived before the thing happens
  ok malformed JSON is refused
  ok a foreign schema is refused
  ok an odd capture dimension is refused before the take, not after
  ok an unparseable region is refused
  ok a screenplay that declares a source second is refused
  ok a screenplay that declares a frame coordinate is refused
  ok a duplicate step id is refused, since a take is keyed by it
  ok emphasis on a targetless hold is refused rather than silently centred
  ok a targets file resolves rectangles
  ok a screenplay whose targets all resolve is ready to record
  ok an unresolved target is named before the take, not after
  ok an inside-out rectangle is refused
  ok a take duration is estimated from the screenplay, quiet wait included (15.8s)
  ok the driver writes a take manifest
  ok the driver measures the recording clock rather than assuming ffmpeg started instantly
  ok the driver refuses a black capture before recording
  ok the brightness statistic is written to a file, because metadata=print logs at info level and would be swallowed by -v error
  ok the statistics filename is relative, because ffmpeg's filter parser treats ':' and '\' as syntax
  ok an unreadable brightness statistic is distinguished from a black frame
  ok the driver clears a restored draft before typing
  ok the driver waits for the app to stop repainting rather than trusting an authored settle
  ok the quiet wait happens before the click, so the click cannot land on a page that is still rendering
  ok a screen that never settles is recorded in the manifest rather than passed off as clean
  ok the OS cursor is not captured, because the drawn one replaces it
  ok the real pointer is glided so the app produces the hover states a viewer will see
  ok pointer samples are read from the OS, not assumed from the target rect
  ok the pointer is marked hidden while typing, so the arrow does not cover the text
  ok Click-At is called with space-separated arguments; PowerShell would pass Click-At(a, b) as a single array
  ok step timing is measured, not hard-coded into the driver
  ok the estimated duration budgets the measured quiet wait, so the recorder cannot stop before the last step
  ok an unsettled status survives the manifest round trip
  ok pointer samples are normalised against the capture region, so a plan survives a change of render size
  ok a hidden pointer sample stays hidden through the manifest
  ok a take without pointer telemetry yields no track, rather than one inferred from the rects
  ok a take manifest carries measured seconds
  ok a take manifest carries the rectangle actually acted on
  ok a take step that ends before it starts is refused

